{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/692548-dragonblooded-crafting-in-the-third-edition","id":692548,"title":"Dragonblooded crafting in the third edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-07T09:21:04-07:00","id":692548,"title":"Dragonblooded crafting in the third edition","content":"I want to apologize in advance if I'm asking this in the wrong place. Rest assured I did my due diligence googling and wasn't able to really find an answer to this question. I would really appreciate anyone shedding some light. Perhaps it's been mentioned in some author q&amp;a or spoiler that I couldn't find. <br /> <br /> In 2e I was always somewhat disappointed by Dragonblooded crafting charms, sure they had some neat effects but beyond the excellency their charms didn't make them much better than the average mortal at artifact creation. Now I know crafting will change a lot in the third edition, which is great. What I'm hopingn to learn is if in the new edition artificer will be a valid design space for terrestrial exalted. Obviously it wouldn't make sense for them to compare to the Solar's in terms of their ability to churn out artifacts-- either from a balance standpoint or from the perspective of the setting, but I'm hoping to learn if they will have charms that enable a sufficiently specialized terrestrial to create mid-tier artifacts (like daiklaives and such) as a matter of course. I've always liked the idea of a grizzled earth aspect serving as an &quot;armorer of heroes&quot; roll, repairing and forging weapons and dispensing sage advice to characters (kind of like totosai if you've seen inu yasha). Sure he might not be able to crank out daiklaives at a clip like a solar can, but perhaps he creates one or two of such remarkable weapons every decade which are prized thoughout the realm. <br /> <br /> Anyway, basically just wondering if that sort of character will be supported by Dragonblooded charms, or if they will more or less be constrained to excelling at mortal crafts and have to mostly rely on their excellency to perform artifact crafting. I can see either scenario working out, and to some degree the second one seems to make more sense in the post apocalyptic landscape of creation in 3e, but I'm still hopeful.<br /> <br /> If anyone knows or can guess at an answer it would be appreciated.<br /> <br /> My apologies for any gross grammatical or spelling errors, typing on my phone and that's no fun for anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T09:36:35-07:00","id":692595,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure Solars should be casually churning out artifacts either! Considering a stated goal of 3e is to make artifacts feel rare and coveted versus a daiklaive being a dime a dozen, I think even Solars are not going to wake up late and knock out a new daiklaive from concept to completion before brunch, even with Charms. <br /> <br /> Remember, in 3e, every daiklaive is unique - and this isn't just the lip service paid in 2e, because every daiklaive has potentially its own Evocation cascade deriving from the materials used in its construction and its crafter's intent, and how it was used over time as well.<br /> <br /> What you're saying probably works, though. There certainly should be Terrestrial artificers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T09:45:15-07:00","id":692631,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I think I phrased it blithely. Let's say a dedicated solar craftsman can knock out a daiklaives every year or two, then my concept might create one-- assuming he is brought the proper components, every 5-6. Not as quickly, but roughly on the same broad timescale. I made the distinction more to indicate that while obviously they can't be nearly as good or as fast as solars (or the setting doesn't work) I hope that they are an extant thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T09:46:21-07:00","id":692634,"title":"","content":"I'm always surprised when people talk about Craft only within it's (Artifact) purview. A Terrestrial Exalted (or any other legendary craftsman) should be able to consistently churn works of art in their field, be it statues, swords, jewelries or any other thing. Artefacts are great and all, but being able to craft a single Daiklave will not help your army when the Tidal Wyld hits, whereas being able to take steel swords and knock the carbon out of it in a few strikes will (because Iron &gt; Wyld). If DBs are specialized in speed-crafting mundane things or repairing/modifying existing equipment I'll be a happy man.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong: DBs should be able to create Daiklaves and Powerbows, but since their purview is mass combat and teamwork, I would be really happy to see charms which allow them to craft enough arrows for their army in an hour, using only a tree stump, a handful of rocks and a dull knife.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T09:50:26-07:00","id":692635,"title":"","content":"I seem to remember that Vance was working on the Dragon Blooded charms and promised that if they weren't universally well received, he would go 9 rounds with Mike Tyson. In fact, I think the Kickstarter to put Tyson on retainer just finished so Vance had better hope people like his work or else he's gonna get slaughtered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T09:51:24-07:00","id":692636,"title":"","content":"I completely agree. I even said I could honestly see it being appropriate for their charms to completely benefit only mortal craft endeavors (yeah he can't build an artifact particularly well but it's pretty neat that he can sculpt a village from stone with his bare hands at quite a clip). However in 2e, they basically only had charm support for mortal crafts (outside of excellencies) and not so much for any magical crafting, I was wondering if the was going to change so that &quot;master magical sword smith&quot; was equally supported as &quot;incredibly gifted architect&quot; or &quot;armorer of mortals&quot; or &quot;artist who makes sculptures out of fire&quot;.<br /> <br /> @anubys: I'm sure I'll like them either way. heck I even liked them in 2e after errata. And as of right now I have literally nothing to complain about heh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T09:57:18-07:00","id":692642,"title":"","content":"There's certainly scope for a Dragon-Blooded to do things with the new artifact crafting system though it remains to be seen how they'll interact with it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T09:58:26-07:00","id":692644,"title":"","content":"It'd be silly if DBs couldn't make artifacts and manses etc...there were just some things that were wholly beyond their kenning, I would say mostly due to SCS spells and Solars having &quot;easier&quot; access to enacting SCS workings that only they could maintain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T10:00:55-07:00","id":692646,"title":"","content":"We don't know.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T10:18:45-07:00","id":692661,"title":"","content":"Kind of a tangent, but I hope that Solar crafting looks less like &quot;make the same artifacts faster&quot; and more like &quot;building superlative wonders that do amazing and unique things nobody else can achieve&quot; which only once in a while are also daiklaves.<br /> <br /> As for Dragon-Blooded, I like Magnum Opus' idea and that's a niche that's not only specially suited to the Dragon-Blooded, it's not really available to less numerous Exalted, without turning factory cathedrals into rapid, mass-production (if that's not what they already are in canon).<br /> <br /> However, I feel like &quot;craft pure cold iron&quot; in specific should be achievable with thaumaturgy, and also that turning iron into steel shouldn't be reversible that easily. I prefer the idea that in Creation, steel is a separate substance transformed by fire rather than an alloy of iron and carbon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T10:59:47-07:00","id":692731,"title":"","content":"My thoughts on Dragonblooded crafting, at the mo', are:<br /> <br /> 1) Ideally, rather than be about artefact level, for one they would have a relatively (genre appropriately) easy time making the sort of idle (but somewhat trival or fragile) sorceries beloved of the decadent sorcerer lords of Melnibone, and the mighty tools of utterly badass elemental samurai. Since those two together are close to what the Dragonblooded Dynasty are like. Then have more of a challenge going outside that.<br /> <br /> 2) I think the limit where the game effectively goes &quot;OK - what you're trying to do with craft is really a civilizational and cultural scale accomplishment, that is beyond the scope of any reasonable crafting system designed to describe the works of a single magical artisan in a game of drama and kung fu action&quot; should come earlier for Dragonblooded than Solars (and also earlier than for certain demons and other forces divine and strange the DBs can call on... for a price). <br /> <br /> At the same time, I'm not interested in the sort of &quot;No way can the united Dragonblooded Host *ever*, repeat *ever*, make one of these world stabilising Jade Obelisks, with any amount of time, resources or circumstances. Here, we've proved it by math with as the mechanics are the physics of the world. You must feel like the Solars are more heroes now, surely?&quot; rhetoric that came up in the 2e fan community about craft. I don't think that sort of overreaching mechanic is very necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T11:12:13-07:00","id":692741,"title":"","content":"Are you asking about crafting for PC or for NPC? The answers are VERY different.<br /> <br /> PC are the exception. They do the impossible, they achieve great things, they do what it was thought could not be done.<br /> <br /> Therefore, if you have a dragonblooded PC, be they focused on crafting, or swording, they are going to be very very good at what they do. They are going to be the exception. They are going to be the never heard of before grand craftsman that turns sand into sawblades.<br /> <br /> If you are asking what the NPC in the setting can do, it's a very different answer. They don't have the time, the skill or the ability to produce on a large scale, you can work that out just by looking at the setting/history.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T11:14:28-07:00","id":692742,"title":"","content":"Eh, when you're talking about Exalted NPCs, the timeframes should be the same. Exalted NPCs are still Exalted and the PCs aren't better than them by fiat. A DB artisan doesn't exist for your PC to casually appear and trounce them without putting forth any real effort. <br /> <br /> It still doesn't mean that a guy has time or resources to stand around making magic swords all day erry day for 50 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T11:14:39-07:00","id":692743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/692548-dragonblooded-crafting-in-the-third-edition?p=692646#post692646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question concerns an unreleased system in an unreleased edition for an unreleased supplement to that edition. Only a writer could elaborate. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T11:26:12-07:00","id":692753,"title":"","content":"Not talking about a large scale (we're talking about 10-20 artifact weapons in a 250-300 year lifespan) anyway. Just idle speculation really though I do think the npc v pc debate is interesting (and I tend to favor zel's point)<br /> <br /> Tikor: not sure what the point your trying to make is. I am grateful to you for pointing out that both the supplement and the system were unreleased, I direct you to the part in my original post where I say: &quot;perhaps it's been mentioned in a spoiler or author q&amp;a that I could not find&quot;. Which is where I figured a definitive answer to my question, if it exists, would be found. I do understand how books work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T11:39:27-07:00","id":692762,"title":"","content":"The biggest challenge that has always faced Dragon Blooded crafters is the fact that it is a central conceit of the game line that the Terrestrial Exalted cannot equal the heights of the First Age.<br /> <br /> Airships, warstriders, artifacts, etc. Most of these, ando the superior versions, were produced back during the First Age.<br /> <br /> The game line has enforced this in various ways - I think back in First Edition Dragon Blooded were almost entirely prohibited from making 4 and 5 dot artifacts. (I might be wrong though, it's been a while).<br /> <br /> I imagine that this concept, that the great works and wonders of the previous Era are largely beyond the ability of the Dragon Blooded to match will still be a thing in 3rd edition. I have no idea though what sort of effect, if any, that this concept will have on how the authors approach Dragonblooded charms. I think that in previous editions, this concept was somewhat responsible for the poor quality of Terrestrial craft charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T11:40:31-07:00","id":692764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/692548-dragonblooded-crafting-in-the-third-edition?p=692661#post692661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of a tangent, but I hope that Solar crafting looks less like &quot;make the same artifacts faster&quot; and more like &quot;building superlative wonders that do amazing and unique things nobody else can achieve&quot; which only once in a while are also daiklaves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of my response to that tangent is: I do sort of think Solars should be crafting artefacts which are very conspicuously An Inspiring Work from the Visionary Mind of A Singular Force of Genius... which you wouldn't imagine fitting from another Exalted, as an image and style, rather than &quot;An artefact is Solar if it has this much power&quot;. At the same time, these *do* need a certain amount of power to actually back up their image. <br /> <br /> If this makes any sense. And how that could be realized through Charms, I dunno.<br /> <br /> Partly this is probably because my go to image of an archetypal Solar Crafter is a bit like a meat version Orichalcum Caste Crafter, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T11:41:51-07:00","id":692766,"title":"","content":"The point was to stay redundantly on-topic, or perhaps to warn against unsourced speculation, or maybe to emphasize the finality of the original question to encourage the tangent afterlife of your thread. It was meant as a detached elaboration, not an accusation. I probably should not have posted since I did not make my context clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T11:44:30-07:00","id":692769,"title":"","content":"Fair enough, sorry for jumping to conclusions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T11:48:14-07:00","id":692771,"title":"","content":"Dragon-Blooded artificers will certainly be a thing in EX3. Making something like Icemind or a Warstrider, now... THAT'S a tall order and a character-defining goal. But daiklaves, armor, hearthstone bracers that will be cherished hundreds of years hence by your descendants? Oh yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T11:52:31-07:00","id":692775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/692548-dragonblooded-crafting-in-the-third-edition?p=692764#post692764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Inspiring Work from the Visionary Mind of A Singular Force of Genius...If this makes any sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/692548-dragonblooded-crafting-in-the-third-edition?p=692764#post692764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how that could be realized through Charms, I dunno.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it needs to be defined through Charms. I'd rather lean on the setting, that in the First Age the Solars were beyond wealthy and in charge of the world. They had the time and the resources and the problems of necessity that would generate such artifacts. By contrast the Sidereals had jobs, the Dragon-Blooded had moderate wealth and time, and I don't frankly know why the Lunars couldn't have matched their brilliance in Artifice with the exception of the Art of Permanence. But when your Artifact can heal itself, does it need to be so Permanent? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T12:07:31-07:00","id":692787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/692548-dragonblooded-crafting-in-the-third-edition?p=692771#post692771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon-Blooded artificers will certainly be a thing in EX3. Making something like Icemind or a Warstrider, now... THAT'S a tall order and a character-defining goal. But daiklaves, armor, hearthstone bracers that will be cherished hundreds of years hence by your descendants? Oh yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sweet! Thanks. And yes that is exactly what I was hoping. Sure no terrestrial is going to casually manufacture first age wonders, sure once in a generation prodigies might occasionally produce a wonder that harkens back to the golden age, but with such effort and so infrequently that it only serves to highlight how far the world has fallen. In the meantime respected Dragonblooded craftsmen might periodically craft magical arms and armor to be awarded to promising scions of their house or to be passed down through the generations-- not a trivial feat, but not something that requires the totality of an exalt's life be dedicated to. Thank you for your answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T15:12:46-07:00","id":692965,"title":"","content":"Crafting in general needs something more to interact with than how long it takes. As for the concept, you certainly need it to be viable if you're going to have somebody like Gavin Bast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}